6. INSTALL AND DEMO MODEL
================================================================================

There are three conceptual install modes:

A. demo
- fastest, no paid services
- acceptable to rely on local cluster or local tooling
- should feel magical

B. core
- intended for real internal POC clusters
- installs minimal viable platform dependencies

C. full
- NOT MVP
- may be stubbed

MVP default installs should be minimal and sane.
Do NOT install a kitchen sink by default.

Recommended MVP install profiles:
- demo:
  - ArgoCD
  - Kargo
  - ingress
- core:
  - ArgoCD
  - Kargo
  - optional ExternalSecrets
  - optional stakater reloader
- full:
  - stub or future

Avoid installing by default in MVP:
- Vault OSS
- ExternalDNS
- cert-manager
- kubeseal
- gateway API as a mandatory default
- KEDA as default
These can be future add-ons.

================================================================================
7. AUTH MODEL
================================================================================

MVP auth starts with **basic admin auth**.

Flow:
- suparship bootstraps a single admin credential
- username default: `admin`
- password generated securely
- password stored only as bcrypt hash in Kubernetes Secret
- plaintext password shown once during bootstrap/reset
- session-based cookie auth for UI/API
- no plaintext password persistence
- no JWT complexity in MVP

Required commands:
- `suparship admin bootstrap`
- `suparship admin reset-password`

Auth modes:
- basic (MVP default)
- google (future/scaffold only)
- possibly disabled/api-only later

Backend auth requirements:
- secure cookie sessions
- HttpOnly cookie
- secure cookie configurable for local dev vs production
- `GET /api/v1/auth/me`
- `POST /api/v1/auth/login`
- `POST /api/v1/auth/logout`

Do NOT:
- store plaintext passwords
- log passwords
- use admin/admin defaults
- implement a giant user management system in MVP

================================================================================
8. ORG / TEAM / RBAC MODEL
================================================================================

For OSS MVP, support a **single default org**.

Important distinction:
- In OSS MVP, org is structure.
- In future SaaS, org is identity/billing/multi-tenancy.

So in MVP:
- include a default org
- include teams
- include basic project RBAC
- do NOT build advanced enterprise tenancy

Roles:
- org_admin
- project_admin
- developer
- viewer

Concepts:
- default org exists by default
- teams are basic grouping objects
- project role bindings map teams to project roles

This should be enough for internal POC rollout.

Do NOT build yet:
- user invitations
- self-serve org switching
- multi-tenant workspace billing
- advanced audit features
- complex cross-org IAM

Google SSO:
- allowed as future config scaffolding
- not required to fully implement right now
- but architecture should leave room for Google Groups-based team mapping later

