11. TEMPLATE SYSTEM
================================================================================

Yes, suparship needs a template system from day one.

Templates are the core abstraction.

A template is:
- rendering engine
- UI schema
- mapping layer

Recommended MVP approach:
- Helm-first
- optional Kustomize overlays later
- suparship metadata layer on top

Each template should include:
- template.yaml
- Helm chart
- values.yaml
- chart templates

Example template layout:
- templates/web-service/template.yaml
- templates/web-service/chart/Chart.yaml
- templates/web-service/chart/values.yaml
- templates/web-service/chart/templates/*.yaml

`template.yaml` must define:
- metadata
- title
- description
- category
- engine
- inputs
- advanced inputs
- secret inputs
- mappings
- presets

Supported input types:
- string
- number
- boolean
- enum
- secret reference

Do NOT expose raw Helm values directly in the UI.
Do expose curated inputs that map to chart values.

Support presets like:
- resources.size = small|medium|large
instead of exposing raw CPU/memory everywhere.

First built-in templates should include:
- web-service
- worker
- cron-job
Later templates may include:
- static site
- private admin tool

For MVP, at least implement web-service well.

================================================================================
12. APP / ENVIRONMENT / COMPONENT MODEL
================================================================================

The primary UX object in suparship is the **app**.

Recommended user-facing hierarchy:
- org
- project
- app
- environment

Recommended internal runtime hierarchy:
- app
- environment instance
- component runtime

This is intentional:

- **project** is a team/workspace boundary
- **app** is the thing a developer creates, previews, promotes, and owns
- **environment** is where the app is running: staging, prod, or preview
- **component** is an internal runtime unit inside the app such as web, worker, cron, or gateway

The product must feel simple for small teams and still work for medium-sized product teams.

Rules:
- app is the default top-level deployment object in the UI
- environment is selected within an app, not treated as the main navigation object
- component is hidden by default unless the template or runtime requires advanced visibility
- preview and promotion are app-scoped, not component-scoped

Examples:
- a simple frontend app may have one default component named `web`
- a medium app may have `web`, `worker`, and `scheduler`
- an advanced app may later expose traffic controls for stable/canary releases

Do NOT force users to model tightly coupled units as many separate services when they ship and promote together.

If existing code or routes still use the term `service` during early MVP implementation, treat it as a temporary implementation detail. The product direction and user-facing model should converge on **app**.
================================================================================
13. APP CREATION MODEL
================================================================================

An app should be created from a template through a form-based UI.

The flow:
- user chooses a template
- UI renders fields from template metadata
- user fills in values
- backend validates input
- backend persists an app spec
- backend generates rendered config inputs for deployment/GitOps

App spec should include:
- project
- template reference
- values
- secret refs
- component definitions or component defaults derived from the template
- environment overrides
- maybe derived/generated metadata

Keep model deterministic and serializable.

Config precedence should be conceptually:
- org
- project
- app
- environment override

App-level fields should generally include:
- name
- template
- curated template values
- component topology
- preview policy
- default route intent

Environment-level fields should generally include:
- deployed release/version
- environment-specific URLs/hostnames
- replica or resource overrides
- traffic policy
- runtime status

Secret values must not be stored in Git.
Secret inputs should default to secret reference mode.

