16. KUBERNETES / GITOPS INTEGRATION
================================================================================

Use Kubernetes and OSS tools as the source of execution.

Expected integrations:
- Kubernetes API for workloads, pods, logs, namespaces, ingresses
- ArgoCD for app/sync/deploy status
- Kargo for promotions

Do not replace these tools.

Runtime mapping guidance:
- one app spec can produce multiple environment instances
- each app environment instance should map cleanly to GitOps state
- for MVP, one namespace per app environment instance is the simplest default
  - examples:
    - `hello-staging`
    - `hello-prod`
    - `hello-pr-182`

Component guidance:
- components belong to the app spec
- component runtime state exists inside each environment instance
- components should not become the primary top-level UX object in MVP

Namespace strategy:
- environment isolation by default
- preview isolation by default
- prefer deterministic app-environment namespace names

Ingress hostname patterns:
- `app.staging.localhost`
- `app.prod.localhost`
- `pr-182.app.preview.localhost`
- `argocd.localhost`

Preview behavior:
- preview is an ephemeral environment instance of an app
- preview should include all preview-enabled components
- heavy or nonessential components may opt out of preview at the template/component layer

Keep preview name sanitization deterministic and tested.

Do not invent a new deployment engine.

